{"id":"23.02.KickTheBuddy","contentHtml":"<p>As a <strong>Unity Developer</strong> at <strong>Playgendary</strong>, I worked on the world-famous hit <code>Kick the Buddy</code>, contributing to the development of one of the key aspects of the game — the weapon arsenal.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My work focused on expanding and supporting content that directly affects core gameplay and the \"juiciness\" of player sensations.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>As part of the project's unification and development, my key task was <strong>porting the existing weapon arsenal from legacy code on <code>Cocos Creator</code> to the main project on <code>Unity</code></strong>.</p>\n<p>This required not just rewriting logic from <code>JavaScript</code> to <code>C#</code>, but <mark>exact recreation of gameplay \"feel\"</mark> (player feel), including physics, timings, and VFX, so that players wouldn't notice the difference.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<p>My workflow included several key stages:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Mechanics Re-engineering:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Conducted <strong>logic deconstruction</strong> of weapons in the source project on <code>Cocos Creator</code>.</li>\n<li>Implemented this logic in <code>C#</code> in <code>Unity</code>, adapting it to the existing architecture of the main project.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Full Weapon Integration Pipeline:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Integrated art assets (sprites, models) and configured physical components (<code>Rigidbody</code>, <code>Colliders</code>) for correct interaction with the character.</li>\n<li>Connected and configured <code>VFX</code> and sound effect systems for each weapon to achieve maximum impact.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Focus on \"Player Feel\":</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Special attention was paid to <mark>exact recreation of \"juiciness\"</mark> of each weapon to preserve the very gaming experience for which players love <code>Kick the Buddy</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Successful Migration:</strong> Dozens of weapons were successfully ported from <code>Cocos Creator</code> to <code>Unity</code>, which helped unify the codebase and simplify further development.</li>\n<li><strong>Preservation of Player Experience:</strong> The migration went seamlessly for players, with full preservation of unique behavior and \"feel\" of each weapon.</li>\n<li><strong>Experience in AAA Studio:</strong> Gained valuable experience working in a large studio on a world-famous product and unique competence in <mark>mechanics re-engineering between different game engines</mark>.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Kick the Buddy","date":"2023-02","type":"project","tagsArray":["Mobile","Casual","Unity","C#","Cocos Creator","JS"],"heroVideo":null,"shortDescription":"<p>Worked at Playgendary on Kick the Buddy. Main task: <mark>porting and re-engineering weapons</mark> from Cocos Creator to Unity while fully preserving the \"player feel\".</p>\n","storeLinks":["https://newplg.dev/","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.playgendary.kickthebuddy","https://apps.apple.com/iq/app/kick-the-buddy/id1278869953"],"role":"team","projectIcon":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/card.mp4?v=1765046944952","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/screenshots/1.webp","width":1080,"height":608},{"src":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/screenshots/2.webp","width":1080,"height":608},{"src":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/screenshots/3.webp","width":1080,"height":608},{"src":"/images/projects/23.02.KickTheBuddy/screenshots/4.webp","width":1080,"height":608}]}